     xmlns:ns="http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:wot="http://xmlns.com/wot/0.1/"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://mklab.iti.gr/pericles/Policy_ODP">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"/>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The pattern intends to model policies, their characteristics and their associated entities, such as processes and agents.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Policy Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal">1. What are the main entities associated with a policy? A policy is usually associated with super/sub-policies, processes, agents and other entities.
2. What are the main attributes of a policy? They are version, language, policy type, requirement level, implementation status and automation status.
3. Where is a policy described? Statements are detailed text (formal or non- formal) definitions of the policy contents.</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>The Policy ODP is expected to facilitate the representation of the policy notion, which can be exploited in various domains. A well-established, comprehensible pattern will prove to be advantageous.</cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The pattern intends to model policies, their characteristics and their associated entities, such as processes and agents.</cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <cpannotationschema:scenarios>Some examples of instantiation of the Policy ODP are:
  1. The policy has two subpolicies
  2. The policy is implemented by a certain process
  3. The policy is validated by a certain process
  4. The policy is assigned to John Smith
  5. The policy is fully automated</cpannotationschema:scenarios>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x8; term declared x8;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Policy Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


